WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:04.007
In part one

2
00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:07.053
a zero dot product meant a right

3
00:00:07.145 --> 00:00:09.544
angle between two vectors.

4
00:00:09.544 --> 00:00:13.420
Now whole subspaces can be perpendicular.

5
00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:16.043
Here is the drone's plane

6
00:00:16.134 --> 00:00:19.043
of reachable places, in R three.

7
00:00:19.043 --> 00:00:21.588
Stand a second plane on it

8
00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:23.770
like a wall on a floor.

9
00:00:23.861 --> 00:00:26.406
The arrows normal to the two

10
00:00:26.497 --> 00:00:28.770
planes are perpendicular

11
00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:31.770
one minus one plus zero is zero.

12
00:00:32.120 --> 00:00:35.054
So are the wall and the floor

13
00:00:35.155 --> 00:00:37.280
orthogonal subspaces?

14
00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:39.000
Pause and think.

15
00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:45.718
Two subspaces are orthogonal when every

16
00:00:45.798 --> 00:00:48.936
vector in one is perpendicular to every

17
00:00:49.017 --> 00:00:50.626
vector in the other.

18
00:00:50.626 --> 00:00:54.166
The drone's plane and the line through one

19
00:00:54.166 --> 00:00:56.580
minus one, one are like that.

20
00:00:56.930 --> 00:01:00.770
Now read A x equals zero one row at a time

21
00:01:00.770 --> 00:01:04.254
x has dot product zero with every row.

22
00:01:04.343 --> 00:01:07.112
So it is perpendicular to every

23
00:01:07.201 --> 00:01:09.702
combination of the rows too

24
00:01:09.791 --> 00:01:12.202
the nullspace is orthogonal

25
00:01:12.292 --> 00:01:13.810
to the row space.

26
00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:17.795
Check it for the drone with basis vectors

27
00:01:17.795 --> 00:01:21.343
the rows of R and the special solutions.

28
00:01:21.343 --> 00:01:24.804
Row one dot the first special solution

29
00:01:24.804 --> 00:01:28.266
minus two plus zero plus two plus zero

30
00:01:28.266 --> 00:01:28.785
zero.

31
00:01:28.785 --> 00:01:30.862
Row one dot the second

32
00:01:30.862 --> 00:01:34.410
one plus zero plus zero minus one, zero.

33
00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:36.401
Row two dot the first

34
00:01:36.401 --> 00:01:39.949
zero minus one plus one plus zero, zero.

35
00:01:39.949 --> 00:01:42.372
And row two dot the second

36
00:01:42.372 --> 00:01:45.920
zero minus one plus zero plus one, zero.

37
00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:49.513
The nullspace is more than orthogonal

38
00:01:49.594 --> 00:01:50.979
to the row space

39
00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:53.910
it holds every vector perpendicular

40
00:01:53.991 --> 00:01:54.969
to the rows.

41
00:01:55.050 --> 00:01:57.574
It is the orthogonal complement

42
00:01:57.656 --> 00:01:59.040
of the row space.

43
00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:01.239
And the dimensions add up

44
00:02:01.239 --> 00:02:04.740
two plus two is four, the whole of R four.

45
00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:06.079
In R three

46
00:02:06.079 --> 00:02:10.035
the drone's plane and the line through one

47
00:02:10.035 --> 00:02:13.271
minus one, one are complements too

48
00:02:13.271 --> 00:02:15.339
two plus one is three.

49
00:02:15.429 --> 00:02:18.935
So a target b is reachable exactly when

50
00:02:19.025 --> 00:02:21.992
it is perpendicular to that line.

51
00:02:21.992 --> 00:02:23.340
One, two, one

52
00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:27.206
one minus two plus one is zero, reachable.

53
00:02:27.206 --> 00:02:28.554
One, one, one

54
00:02:28.554 --> 00:02:31.341
one minus one plus one is one

55
00:02:31.341 --> 00:02:32.690
not reachable.

56
00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:34.720
Back to the puzzle.

57
00:02:34.720 --> 00:02:36.780
It is tempting to say yes

58
00:02:36.857 --> 00:02:38.841
because the wall meets the

59
00:02:38.917 --> 00:02:40.672
floor at a right angle.

60
00:02:40.748 --> 00:02:43.038
But two planes through zero in

61
00:02:43.114 --> 00:02:45.251
R three always share a line.

62
00:02:45.251 --> 00:02:48.608
Here it is the line through minus one, one

63
00:02:48.608 --> 00:02:49.108
two.

64
00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:51.857
That vector lies in both planes

65
00:02:51.936 --> 00:02:54.374
and its dot product with itself

66
00:02:54.453 --> 00:02:57.678
is one plus one plus four: six, not zero.

67
00:02:57.757 --> 00:03:00.667
A vector in both subspaces would have

68
00:03:00.746 --> 00:03:03.106
to be perpendicular to itself

69
00:03:03.106 --> 00:03:05.780
so the planes are not orthogonal.

70
00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:07.904
The dimensions say it too

71
00:03:07.904 --> 00:03:10.500
two plus two is more than three.

72
00:03:11.080 --> 00:03:15.045
Every recipe of button presses splits into

73
00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:18.727
a row space part and a nullspace part.

74
00:03:18.727 --> 00:03:22.881
Take one press of u and one of v: x is one

75
00:03:22.881 --> 00:03:24.486
one, zero, zero

76
00:03:24.486 --> 00:03:28.640
and it flies the drone to two, five, three.

77
00:03:28.990 --> 00:03:32.569
Its row space part is two, five, nine

78
00:03:32.569 --> 00:03:34.735
three, over seventeen.

79
00:03:34.735 --> 00:03:38.408
Its nullspace part is fifteen, twelve

80
00:03:38.408 --> 00:03:42.269
minus nine, minus three, over seventeen.

81
00:03:42.269 --> 00:03:45.377
The nullspace part does nothing

82
00:03:45.377 --> 00:03:49.615
A times x equals A times the row space part

83
00:03:49.615 --> 00:03:51.310
two, five, three.

84
00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:54.924
Draw the flat plane through the two parts

85
00:03:54.924 --> 00:03:57.099
they meet at a right angle.

86
00:03:57.099 --> 00:03:58.265
By Pythagoras

87
00:03:58.343 --> 00:04:00.674
seven seventeenths plus twenty

88
00:04:00.752 --> 00:04:02.772
seven seventeenths is two

89
00:04:02.772 --> 00:04:04.715
the length squared of x.

90
00:04:04.715 --> 00:04:06.502
So the row space part

91
00:04:06.502 --> 00:04:09.144
with length about point six four

92
00:04:09.144 --> 00:04:12.330
is the shortest recipe that reaches two

93
00:04:12.330 --> 00:04:13.340
five, three.

94
00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:15.515
In machine learning

95
00:04:15.515 --> 00:04:17.906
things are stored as vectors

96
00:04:17.906 --> 00:04:20.537
and similar means a small angle.

97
00:04:20.617 --> 00:04:23.487
Cosine similarity is the dot product

98
00:04:23.567 --> 00:04:25.480
divided by both lengths.

99
00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:29.825
Each café drink is its column of ratings.

100
00:04:29.825 --> 00:04:32.553
Tea is two, zero, one, one

101
00:04:32.553 --> 00:04:35.963
and cocoa is four, zero, two, two

102
00:04:35.963 --> 00:04:39.081
cosine one, the same direction.

103
00:04:39.081 --> 00:04:42.881
Latte and mocha: point nine seven six

104
00:04:42.881 --> 00:04:43.563
close.

105
00:04:43.563 --> 00:04:47.558
Espresso and tea: point four zero eight

106
00:04:47.558 --> 00:04:48.630
far apart.

107
00:04:48.980 --> 00:04:52.126
But cocoa is twice as long as tea.

108
00:04:52.126 --> 00:04:55.272
Cosine similarity ignores length

109
00:04:55.364 --> 00:04:57.585
a cosine of one does not

110
00:04:57.677 --> 00:04:59.620
mean the same vector.

111
00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.677
So: the row space and the nullspace

112
00:05:02.748 --> 00:05:04.659
are orthogonal complements

113
00:05:04.729 --> 00:05:06.640
and so are the column space

114
00:05:06.711 --> 00:05:08.339
and the left nullspace.

115
00:05:08.339 --> 00:05:11.382
Every recipe splits into a row space part

116
00:05:11.382 --> 00:05:14.425
which does the work, and a nullspace part

117
00:05:14.425 --> 00:05:15.840
which does nothing.

118
00:05:16.190 --> 00:05:19.068
Two planes in R three are never

119
00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:22.873
orthogonal subspaces: they share a line.

120
00:05:22.873 --> 00:05:26.772
And cosine similarity measures direction

121
00:05:26.772 --> 00:05:27.886
not length.

122
00:05:27.886 --> 00:05:32.063
Your turn: split the recipe zero, two, zero

123
00:05:32.063 --> 00:05:33.084
minus one.

124
00:05:33.084 --> 00:05:35.590
Next lecture: projections.
